Preamble
--------
Through this CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Weakly Reciprocal
("CERN-OHL-W"), CERN wishes to support the open hardware community by
providing an appropriate legal framework for the collaboration,
development and exploitation of hardware designs. It is the intent of
CERN that this Licence can be used by anyone to share hardware
designs. It applies to hardware design files including, but not
limited to, schematic diagrams, layouts, circuit board designs, FPGA
and ASIC register-transfer level (RTL) files, and mechanical designs.

1. Definitions
--------------
1.1 "Licence" means this CERN-OHL-W.
1.2 "Source" means information such as design files or documentation
    which can be used to make Physical Products or other Source.
1.3 "Covered Source" means Source that is accompanied by a Recipient Copy,
    or that has been released under this Licence.
1.4 "Product" means any good produced from Source, whether in physical
    form or in the form of FPGA or ASIC gate-level netlists or bitstreams.
1.5 "You" means an individual or legal entity exercising rights under this Licence.

2. Grant of Rights
------------------
2.1 You may copy and distribute verbatim copies of the Covered Source,
    provided that You keep intact all copyright notices, author attributions,
    and references to the Department of Computer Engineering, University of Tripoli.
2.2 You may modify the Covered Source and distribute Your modifications under
    the terms of this Licence, provided that You prominently label the Source
    with notices indicating that You changed the files and giving the date of any change.
2.3 You must provide proper academic attribution in any publication, technical report,
    or derivative hardware architecture that incorporates, builds upon, or adapts
    this L2 BDI Compressed Cache RTL design or its mathematical compression logic.

3. Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability
-------------------------------------------------------
3.1 The Covered Source is provided strictly "AS IS", without warranty of any kind,
    express or implied, including, but not limited to, the warranties of
    merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.
3.2 In no event shall the Authors, Contributors, or University of Tripoli be liable
    for any claim, damages or other liability, whether in an action of contract,
    tort or otherwise, arising from, out of or in connection with the Covered Source
    or the use or other dealings in the Covered Source.
